SHORYUKEN is released under the Zero-Clause BSD license (0BSD): no attribution, no
notice preservation, no conditions.

That covers the code written for this project: everything under main/, host/,
tools/, components/audio_hal, components/display, components/imu,
components/medal_input and components/medalboot, knobs.cmake, and the files
core/cps1.c, core/cps1.h, core/cps1_internal.h, core/cps1_mem.h,
core/cps1_view.h, core/cps1_video.c, core/cps1_sound.c, core/cps1_idle.c,
core/ym2151.c, core/ym2151.h, core/okim6295.c and core/okim6295.h.

It does not cover:

- core/z80/, which is Marat Fayzullin's emulator and is non-commercial only;
- core/m68k/, which is Karl Stenerud's Musashi, under the MIT license;
- core/ym2151_tables.h, which is copied from Aaron Giles' ymfm, under the
  BSD-3-Clause license.

Because of the first of those, a built SHORYUKEN image may be shared but not
sold.

It does not cover the game ROMs, which are not distributed here and never will
be. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for the code this project is derived from.

